              {
                "kind": "circle",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 150,
                "r": 110,
                "fill": "orange"
              },
              {
                "kind": "circle",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 150,
                "r": 55,
                "fill": "yellow",
                "label": "DNA or RNA"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 20,
                "text": "envelope",
                "size": 20,
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true,
                "change": "add"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Viruses only copy themselves inside a host cell, using its ribosomes.",
          "write": "obligate intracellular parasite"
        },
        {
          "say": "So antibiotics, which hit cell walls and 70S ribosomes, do nothing to viruses.",
          "write": "antibiotics ✗ viruses"
        },
        {
          "say": "A prion is a misfolded protein that makes normal proteins misfold too.",
          "write": "prion = misfolded protein",
